      {
        "id": 127955,
        "name": "cmschex",
        "username": "cmschex",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/e9bcb4/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-21T15:15:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Flintlock\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/flintlock/48/2183_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Flintlock:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Even following the rules, he has yet to impress our group as far as challenges go.Then again, the first time we fought him, I might have Mistbound him for five out of the six turns it took to K.O. him. Yeah…not allowed to do that again.Second time was without shenanigans, but we had consistent ongoing removal on the table which, as mentioned, seriously hamstrings his game plan. He still came off as pretty easily handled.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Mistbound any villain in the game for 5 turns and let me know how difficult they are. &nbsp;Deadline falls into that category of 3 difficulty villains who have a specific weakness (in his case ongoing destruction). &nbsp;Honestly, now that I've played all the final production versions, I think Infinitor is harder on average (especially on Advanced, that's an insane battle)</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:02:39.064Z",
